questions.explanation:
Multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate \(\sqrt{x+4}+2\):
\[
\frac{\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x}
=
\frac{(\sqrt{x+4}-2)(\sqrt{x+4}+2)}
{x(\sqrt{x+4}+2)}
=
\frac{x+4-4}{x(\sqrt{x+4}+2)}.
\]
Thus
\[
\frac{\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x}
=
\frac{x}{x(\sqrt{x+4}+2)}
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt{x+4}+2}
\]
for \(x\neq0\). Therefore,
\[
\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x}
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt{4}+2}
=
\frac{1}{4}.
\]
